 "finding": "THE EDGE IS ROUTABLE AND ITS WHOLE PRICE IS ONE NAMED OBJECT: the GND B.Cu island-31 bond neck, 10.282 mm2 bonding exactly C4.2 and U3.12, severed 4.790 + 4.724 mm2 across a 0.150 mm neck.  Every unguarded route -- 85.843 mm / 4 barrels at --grid 100000, 86.317 mm at 50000, identical at --via-cost 6 -- splits that same island and nothing else, and closes the edge (open retained NETS 21 -> 20) at exactly zero net edge gain (43 -> 43) because GND takes one back.  Reserve that ONE tube and the net is NO_PATH at 100000, 50000 AND 25000 nm: the only corridor this board offers to J8.3 runs through the neck.  And the cure is refused by geometry, not by policy -- U3.12 takes NO barrel: NO_VIA_SITE at the 0.600 mm netclass via, at the 0.500 mm DRU floor via, and at 14.0 mm of locality, and the automatic --repair-planes pass fails on the same pad.  U3.12 is why pour_bond_guard.py guards this island in the first place (D-585).",
